issue_context.body:
Hi,

We have some certificates in our system, where we want to use the Subject CommonName (CN=). On Windows we get the expected value, but on linux (ubuntu 18) we get a hexstring of the raw data back. I have narrowed it down to AsnEncodedData (and AsnFormatter), with this little sample:

```
var rawDataString = "3071310B300906035504061302444B31293027060355040A0C20496E67656E206F7267616E697361746F7269736B2074696C6B6E79746E696E673137301006035504030C094A6F686E204A6F686E30230603550405131C58595A3A313131312D323232322D332D343434343434343434343434";
var rawDataBytes = Enumerable.Range(0, rawDataString.Length)
  .Where(x => x % 2 == 0)
  .Select(x => Convert.ToByte(rawDataString.Substring(x, 2), 16))
  .ToArray();

  var asnData = new AsnEncodedData(new Oid("2.5.4.3"), rawDataBytes); // CN=John John
  Console.WriteLine($"CommonName={asnData.Format(false)}");
```

The DN is `CN=John John + SERIALNUMBER=XYZ:1111-2222-3-444444444444, O=Ingen organisatorisk tilknytning, C=DK` .

The problem seems related to https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/15463. So are these multicomponent RDNs not supported on linux or?

Cheers, Frank

---

# API Proposal

```C#
namespace System.Security.Cryptography.X509Certificates
{
    public partial class X500DistinguishedName
    {
        // Reversed defaults to `true` to match the display order from the Name property.
        // It is the reverse of their encoded order, and named to match
        // X500DistinguishedNameFlags.Reversed
        IEnumerable<X500RelativeDistinguishedName> EnumerateRelativeDistinguishedNames(bool reversed = true);
    }

    public sealed class X500RelativeDistinguishedName
    {
        internal X500RelativeDistinguishedName() { }
        
        // If all else fails, send this to AsnReader.
        public ReadOnlyMemory<byte> RawData { get; }
        
        // true is rare, and means all else has failed.
        [MemberNotNullWhen(false, nameof(SingleValueType))]
        public bool HasMultipleValues { get; }

        // null if HasMultipleValues is true
        public Oid? SingleValueType { get; }

        // throws if HasMultipleValues is true, returns null if string is
        // not an appropriate type per the payload.
        public string? GetSingleValueValue() { throw null; }
    }
}
```

## Usage

```C#
private const string CommonNameOid = "2.5.4.3";

private static string GetCommonName(X509Certificate2 cert)
{
    IEnumerable<X500RelativeDistinguishedName> rdns = cert.SubjectName.EnumerateRelativeDistinguishedNames();

    if (rdns.Any(rdn => rdn.HasMultipleValues))
    {
        throw new InvalidOperationException();
    }

    X500RelativeDistinguishedName commonName = rdns.Single(rdn => rdn.SingleValueType!.Value == CommonNameOid);

    return commonName.GetSingleValueValue() ?? throw new InvalidOperationException();
}
```

